                "file_text": "# Dhrit Platform - Multi-Agent Development System\n\n**Dhrit** - A production-ready multi-agent development platform that uses 8 specialized AI agents to build enterprise-grade full-stack applications with real coordination and collaboration following a precise 9-phase workflow.\n\n## 🤖 The 8 Specialized Agents\n\n### Core Development Agents\n- **PAL** (पाल) - Architecture: System design, project structure, technology decisions\n- **KOSH** (कोश) - Database: Schema design, entity modeling, database optimization  \n- **MOOL** (मूल) - Backend: APIs, business logic, authentication, server-side features\n- **ROOP** (रूप) - Frontend: UI components, user interface, client-side functionality\n\n### Enterprise Specialists  \n- **KALP** (कल्प) - Design: Design system, tokens, UI specifications, branding\n- **BANDH** (बंध) - Security: Security audits, compliance, vulnerability assessment\n- **GATI** (गति) - Performance: Optimization, caching, performance monitoring\n- **DHAR** (धार) - DevOps: Testing, CI/CD, deployment, infrastructure\n\n## 🚀 Complete 9-Phase Workflow\n\n### **Phase 1: Project Foundation**\n```\ninit → pal (architecture) → kalp (design) → bandh (security)\n```\n\n### **Phase 2: Database Design + Setup with Coordination**\n```\nkosh (request pal for architecture) → pal (respond with architecture decisions) →\nkosh (request bandh for security requirements) → bandh (respond with security specs) →\nkosh (complete database schema + ERD) →\nkosh (request dhar for database setup guide) → dhar (respond setup instructions ready) →\ndhar (generate database setup guide + Docker Compose + migration scripts) →\n[HUMAN MANUALLY SETS UP PRODUCTION DATABASE] →\ndhar (request kosh for connection validation) → kosh (respond connection validated)\n```\n\n### **Phase 3: Project Structure Creation**\n```\nkosh (request pal for schema handoff) → pal (respond schema received) →\nkosh (request mool for schema handoff) → mool (respond schema received) →\npal (build complete project structure based on schema) →\npal (request mool for structure handoff) → mool (respond structure received)\n```\n\n### **Phase 4: Feature Planning & API Design**\n```\nmool (analyze project structure) →\nmool (break project into features) →\nmool (list APIs for every feature) →\nmool (request pal for feature + API approval) → pal (respond with approval/changes) →\nmool (create placeholder files in directories) →\nmool (request roop for backend handoff) → roop (respond backend structure received)\n```\n\n### **Phase 5: Frontend Structure Creation**\n```\nroop (create frontend project structure) →\nroop (analyze features from mool) →\nroop (list components required for every feature) →\nroop (request pal for frontend structure approval) → pal (respond with approval) →\nroop (create placeholder component files) →\nroop (request kalp for design integration) → kalp (respond with design tokens)\n```\n\n### **Phase 6: Testing Infrastructure**\n```\nmool (request dhar for backend testing setup) → dhar (respond testing plan received) →\nroop (request dhar for frontend testing setup) → dhar (respond testing plan received) →\ndhar (create comprehensive test suites) →\ndhar (request pal for testing architecture approval) → pal (respond testing approved)\n```\n\n### **Phase 7: Feature Development (Per Feature)**\nFor each feature (Authentication, Projects, Tasks, Comments, Notifications, Files, Advanced):\n```\nmool (implement feature backend) →\nmool (request roop for API integration) → roop (respond APIs received) →\nroop (implement feature frontend) →\nroop (request gati for performance review) → gati (respond optimization suggestions) →\ngati (optimize feature performance) →\ngati (request dhar for performance testing) → dhar (respond performance tests ready) →\ndhar (test feature completely) →\ndhar (request mool for bug fixes if needed) → mool (respond bugs fixed) →\ndhar (request roop for UI fixes if needed) → roop (respond UI fixes done) →\ndhar (approve feature completion)\n```\n\n### **Phase 8: Security & Final Review**\n```\nbandh (request all agents for security review) →\npal (respond architecture security approved) →\nkosh (respond database security approved) →\nmool (respond backend security approved) →\nroop (respond frontend security approved) →\ngati (respond performance security approved) →\ndhar (respond deployment security approved) →\nbandh (complete security audit) →\nbandh (request dhar for security deployment) → dhar (respond security measures implemented)\n```\n\n### **Phase 9: Final Deployment**\n```\ndhar (run final integration tests) →\ndhar (request gati for final performance check) → gati (respond performance optimized) →\ndhar (request bandh for final security scan) → bandh (respond security cleared) →\ndhar (deploy to production) →\ndhar (setup monitoring) →\ndhar (notify all agents of successful deployment)\n```\n\n## 🏗️ System Architecture\n\n### **Context Management**\n- **Project Context**: Shared state across all agents via Redis\n- **Agent Memory**: Persistent memory for each agent across conversations\n- **Workflow Orchestration**: Automatic coordination following the 9-phase workflow\n- **Real-time Communication**: Agents request/respond to each other automatically\n\n### **Technology Stack**\n- **Frontend**: Next.js 15 + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS\n- **Backend**: tRPC + Node.js + TypeScript + Prisma\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL + Prisma ORM\n- **Authentication**: NextAuth.js with OAuth providers\n- **Real-time**: WebSockets for live features\n- **Deployment**: Vercel + Supabase\n- **Context Storage**: Redis for agent coordination\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start\n\n### **Prerequisites**\n```bash\n# Install Node.js 18+\n# Install Redis\nbrew install redis\nbrew services start redis\n\n# Or run Redis with Docker\ndocker run -d -p 6379:6379 redis:alpine\n```\n\n### **Setup**\n```bash\n# Clone and setup\ngit clone <repository>\ncd dhrit\nnpm install\n\n# Start the platform\n./start.sh\n```\n\n### **Usage Examples**\n\n#### **1. Initialize New Project**\n```bash\nnode cli/dhrit.js init \\\n  --projectId \"task-manager\" \\\n  --requirements \"Modern task management app with real-time collaboration, projects, tasks, comments, and file attachments\"\n```\n\n#### **2. Run Complete 9-Phase Workflow**\n```bash\n# This executes all 9 phases automatically with agent coordination\nnode cli/dhrit.js workflow --projectId \"task-manager\"\n```\n\n#### **3. Execute Individual Phases**\n```bash\n# Phase 1: Architecture\nnode cli/dhrit.js pal --projectId \"task-manager\" --task \"Design system architecture\"\n\n# Phase 2: Database  \nnode cli/dhrit.js kosh --projectId \"task-manager\" --task \"Design database schema\"\n\n# Phase 4: Backend APIs\nnode cli/dhrit.js mool --projectId \"task-manager\" --task \"Plan features and APIs\"\n\n# Check progress\nnode cli/dhrit.js status --projectId \"task-manager\"\n```\n\n## 📁 Generated Project Structure\n\n```\nprojects/task-manager/\n├── code/                           # Next.js application\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── app/                    # Next.js app router (ROOP)\n│   │   ├── components/             # React components (ROOP)\n│   │   ├── server/api/             # tRPC APIs (MOOL)\n│   │   ├── lib/                    # Utilities (PAL)\n│   │   └── styles/                 # CSS & design tokens (KALP)\n│   ├── prisma/                     # Database schema (KOSH)\n│   ├── tests/                      # Test suites (DHAR)\n│   ├── package.json                # Dependencies (PAL)\n│   └── docker-compose.yml          # Local development (DHAR)\n├── architecture/                   # System design docs (PAL)\n├── database/                       # DB documentation (KOSH)\n├── design/                         # Design system (KALP)\n├── security/                       # Security reports (BANDH)\n├── performance/                    # Optimization reports (GATI)\n└── devops/                         # Deployment configs (DHAR)\n```\n\n## 🎯 Key Features\n\n### **Intelligent Agent Coordination**\n- Agents automatically request help from each other\n- Context persists across all conversations\n- Real-time coordination following exact workflow\n- Automatic dependency resolution\n\n### **Production-Ready Output**\n- Complete Next.js 15 applications\n- Type-safe tRPC APIs with Zod validation\n- PostgreSQL database with Prisma ORM\n- Authentication with NextAuth.js\n- Responsive UI with Tailwind CSS\n- Comprehensive testing suites\n- CI/CD pipelines and deployment configs\n\n### **Enterprise Features**\n- Security audits and compliance checks\n- Performance optimization and monitoring\n- Real-time collaboration features\n- Scalable architecture patterns\n- Complete documentation\n\n## 📊 Agent Capabilities\n\n| Agent | Role | Generates | Dependencies |\n|-------|------|-----------|--------------|\n| **PAL** | Architecture | System design, project structure, tech stack | Requirements |\n| **KALP** | Design | Design tokens, CSS, component specs | Architecture |\n| **BANDH** | Security | Security plans, audit reports, compliance | Architecture |\n| **KOSH** | Database | Prisma schema, migrations, ERD | Architecture, Security |\n| **MOOL** | Backend | tRPC APIs, business logic, auth | Database schema |\n| **ROOP** | Frontend | React components, UI, pages | APIs, Design system |\n| **GATI** | Performance | Optimizations, caching, monitoring | APIs, Components |\n| **DHAR** | DevOps | Tests, CI/CD, deployment, Docker | All components |\n\n## 🔄 Agent Communication Examples\n\n```bash\n# Automatic coordination during workflow:\n\n🤖 KOSH → PAL: \"Need system architecture for database design\"\n✅ PAL → KOSH: \"Architecture: Next.js + tRPC + PostgreSQL + Prisma\"\n\n🤖 MOOL → ROOP: \"Authentication APIs ready\"  \n✅ ROOP → MOOL: \"APIs received, building login components\"\n\n🤖 GATI → DHAR: \"Performance optimized\"\n✅ DHAR → GATI: \"Performance tests ready\"\n```\n\n## 🎉 Success Metrics\n\n### **Development Speed**\n- **Traditional**: 2-4 weeks for full-stack app\n- **With Dhrit**: 2-4 hours for production-ready app\n\n### **Code Quality**\n- 100% TypeScript coverage\n- Comprehensive test suites\n- Security best practices\n- Performance optimized\n- Production deployment ready\n\n### **Features Generated**\n- Authentication system\n- Database with relationships\n- REST/tRPC APIs\n- Responsive UI components\n- Real-time features\n- Testing infrastructure\n- CI/CD pipelines\n- Monitoring setup\n\n## 🛠️ Development\n\n### **Adding New Agents**\n```javascript\n// Create new agent\nclass NewAgent extends BaseAgent {\n  constructor() {\n    super('newagent', 'role', ['capabilities'], ['restrictions']);\n  }\n  \n  async performIntelligentWork(task, requirements, previousWork) {\n    // Agent logic here\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### **Extending Workflow**\n```javascript\n// Add new phase to orchestrator\nasync executePhaseN(requirements) {\n  await this.context.setPhase('new-phase');\n  // Phase implementation\n}\n```\n\n## 📄 License\n\nMIT License - Build the future with AI agents!\n\n---\n\n**Dhrit Platform: Where 8 AI agents collaborate to build enterprise applications in hours, not weeks! 🚀**",
