    "Excellent question! This is the core of intelligent agent coordination. Let me show you how agents will know **what to ask**, **whom to ask**, and **how to ask**:\n\n## **Agent Knowledge System**\n\n### **1. Agent Capability Registry**\n```javascript\n// Each agent declares what it provides and needs\nconst AGENT_CAPABILITIES = {\n  kosh: {\n    provides: ['database-schema', 'entity-models', 'relationships', 'migrations'],\n    needs: ['requirements', 'architecture-decisions'],\n    expertise: 'database-design'\n  },\n  mool: {\n    provides: ['apis', 'business-logic', 'authentication', 'validation'],\n    needs: ['database-schema', 'entity-models', 'security-requirements'],\n    expertise: 'backend-development'\n  },\n  roop: {\n    provides: ['ui-components', 'frontend-logic', 'user-interface'],\n    needs: ['apis', 'design-system', 'component-specs'],\n    expertise: 'frontend-development'\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### **2. Intelligent Need Detection**\n```javascript\nclass MoolAgent extends BaseAgent {\n  async execute(task, requirements, projectId) {\n    await this.initializeContext(projectId);\n    \n    // Analyze what I need to complete this task\n    const needs = await this.analyzeNeeds(task, requirements);\n    \n    // Get what I need from other agents or context\n    const dependencies = await this.resolveDependencies(needs);\n    \n    // Generate code with all dependencies\n    const result = await this.generateWithDependencies(dependencies);\n    \n    return result;\n  }\n  \n  async analyzeNeeds(task, requirements) {\n    const needs = [];\n    \n    // If task involves database operations, I need schema\n    if (this.involvesDatabase(task, requirements)) {\n      needs.push({\n        type: 'database-schema',\n        reason: 'Need entity models for API generation',\n        urgency: 'high'\n      });\n    }\n    \n    // If task involves authentication, I need security requirements\n    if (this.involvesAuth(task, requirements)) {\n      needs.push({\n        type: 'security-requirements',\n        reason: 'Need security specs for auth implementation',\n        urgency: 'high'\n      });\n    }\n    \n    return needs;\n  }\n  \n  involvesDatabase(task, requirements) {\n    const dbKeywords = ['api', 'crud', 'data', 'model', 'entity', 'database'];\n    return dbKeywords.some(keyword => \n      task.toLowerCase().includes(keyword) || \n      requirements.toLowerCase().includes(keyword)\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### **3. Dependency Resolution System**\n```javascript\nclass DependencyResolver {\n  constructor(projectId) {\n    this.projectId = projectId;\n    this.context = new ProjectContext(projectId);\n  }\n  \n  async resolve(needs) {\n    const resolved = {};\n    \n    for (const need of needs) {\n      // First, check if it's already in project context\n      const cached = await this.getCachedDependency(need.type);\n      if (cached) {\n        resolved[need.type] = cached;\n        continue;\n      }\n      \n      // Find which agent can provide this\n      const provider = this.findProvider(need.type);\n      if (!provider) {\n        throw new Error(`No agent can provide: ${need.type}`);\n      }\n      \n      // Request from the provider agent\n      resolved[need.type] = await this.requestFromAgent(provider, need);\n    }\n    \n    return resolved;\n  }\n  \n  findProvider(needType) {\n    for (const [agentName, capabilities] of Object.entries(AGENT_CAPABILITIES)) {\n      if (capabilities.provides.includes(needType)) {\n        return agentName;\n      }\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n  \n  async requestFromAgent(agentName, need) {\n    console.log(`🤖 MOOL requesting ${need.type} from ${agentName.toUpperCase()}`);\n    \n    // Check if the provider agent has already generated this\n    const agentContext = new AgentContext(agentName, this.projectId);\n    const existing = await agentContext.getMemory(need.type);\n    \n    if (existing) {\n      console.log(`✅ Found existing ${need.type} from ${agentName.toUpperCase()}`);\n      return existing;\n    }\n    \n    // Agent hasn't generated it yet, trigger the agent\n    console.log(`🔄 Triggering ${agentName.toUpperCase()} to generate ${need.type}`);\n    return await this.triggerAgentGeneration(agentName, need);\n  }\n  \n  async triggerAgentGeneration(agentName, need) {\n    const agentMap = {\n      kosh: () => new (require('./kosh-agent.js').KoshAgent)(),\n      bandh: () => new (require('./bandh-agent.js').BandhAgent)(),\n      kalp: () => new (require('./kalp-agent.js').KalpAgent)()\n    };\n    \n    const agent = agentMap[agentName]();\n    \n    // Generate appropriate task for the agent\n    const task = this.generateTaskForNeed(need);\n    const requirements = await this.context.getRequirements();\n    \n    const result = await agent.execute(task, requirements, this.projectId);\n    \n    return this.extractNeededData(result, need.type);\n  }\n  \n  generateTaskForNeed(need) {\n    const taskMap = {\n      'database-schema': 'Design database schema',\n      'security-requirements': 'Define security requirements',\n      'design-system': 'Create design system',\n      'entity-models': 'Generate entity models'\n    };\n    \n    return taskMap[need.type] || `Generate ${need.type}`;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### **4. Automatic Agent Triggering**\n```javascript\nclass MoolAgent extends BaseAgent {\n  async resolveDependencies(needs) {\n    const resolver = new DependencyResolver(this.context.projectId);\n    return await resolver.resolve(needs);\n  }\n  \n  async generateWithDependencies(dependencies) {\n    console.log('🧠 MOOL generating with dependencies:', Object.keys(dependencies));\n    \n    // Now I have everything I need\n    if (dependencies['database-schema']) {\n      const schema = dependencies['database-schema'];\n      console.log('📊 Using schema with entities:', schema.entities?.map(e => e.name));\n      \n      // Generate APIs based on actual schema entities\n      return this.generateAPIsFromSchema(schema);\n    }\n    \n    // Fallback to template-based generation\n    return this.generateFromTemplates();\n  }\n  \n  generateAPIsFromSchema(schema) {\n    const files = [];\n    \n    // Generate router for each entity in schema\n    schema.entities.forEach(entity => {\n      const router = this.generateEntityRouter(entity, schema.relationships);\n      files.push({\n        path: `src/server/api/routers/${entity.name.toLowerCase()}.ts`,\n        content: router\n      });\n    });\n    \n    // Generate root router that imports all entity routers\n    const rootRouter = this.generateRootRouter(schema.entities);\n    files.push({\n      path: 'src/server/api/root.ts',\n      content: rootRouter\n    });\n    \n    return { files };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## **Real Example Flow**\n\n### **User Request:**\n```bash\nmool --projectId \"blog-app\" --task \"Create blog APIs\" --requirements \"Blog with posts, comments, and categories\"\n```\n\n### **What Happens:**\n```javascript\n// 1. Mool analyzes needs\nconst needs = [\n  { type: 'database-schema', reason: 'Need Post, Comment, Category models' }\n];\n\n// 2. Mool checks: \"Who provides database-schema?\"\n// Answer: KOSH\n\n// 3. Mool checks: \"Does Kosh already have schema for blog-app?\"\nconst existing = await koshContext.getMemory('database-schema');\n// Answer: No\n\n// 4. Mool triggers Kosh\nconsole.log('🤖 MOOL requesting database-schema from KOSH');\nconst kosh = new KoshAgent();\nconst result = await kosh.execute(\n  'Design database schema', \n  'Blog with posts, comments, and categories', \n  'blog-app'\n);\n\n// 5. Kosh generates schema\n// Kosh analyzes: \"Blog needs Post, Comment, Category, User entities\"\n// Kosh creates: Prisma schema with relationships\n\n// 6. Mool gets the schema\nconst schema = result.schema; // { entities: [Post, Comment, Category, User], relationships: [...] }\n\n// 7. Mool generates APIs based on actual entities\nconst apis = [\n  'src/server/api/routers/posts.ts',    // CRUD